# Task B4.12: OpenCode on Windows on Arm, measured on the Windows VM (admin@192.168.65.3, Win11 ARM64,
# Windows NT 10.0.26100, npm 11.19.0, node v24.20.0) on 2026-10-17 (UTC 17:36-17:49).
#
# Method (controller rulings): nothing is installed globally. Every candidate goes into its own prefix under
# C:\work\b4\oc-*. The admin profile's global OpenCode (used by C:\work\e2e) is read, never changed.
# `ssh -t` gives no screen to read, so each binary runs inside a fresh pseudo console (kernel32 CreatePseudoConsole,
# 120x32) from a PowerShell script (C:\work\b4\cap\capture.ps1, removed afterwards). The script captures every byte
# the console emits, waits 15 s (or until the process exits), sends Ctrl+C, waits 3 s, then closes the console.
# OpenCode's own state is kept off the admin profile: XDG_DATA_HOME / XDG_CONFIG_HOME / XDG_STATE_HOME / XDG_CACHE_HOME
# point to C:\work\b4\oc-home, the working folder is C:\work\b4\oc-proj, and OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE=1.
# "Draws" means: alternate-screen or other TUI escape sequences, and no bun:ffi error, within 15 s.
# Raw captures below are escaped: \e = ESC, \a = BEL, \r \n literal; long runs are shown as <N spaces> and
# <N x ESC[K CRLF>.

