## 1.4 Whether npm installs the x64 build on Arm (own prefix, not -g)
$ ssh admin@192.168.65.3 "mkdir C:\work\b4\oc-cpu & cd /d C:\work\b4 && npm i --prefix C:\work\b4\oc-cpu opencode-ai@1.19.3 --cpu=x64"
npm error code 1
npm error path C:\work\b4\oc-cpu\node_modules\opencode-ai
npm error command failed
npm error command C:\WINDOWS\system32\cmd.exe /d /s /c node ./postinstall.mjs
npm error It seems your package manager failed to install the right opencode CLI package. Try manually installing "opencode-windows-arm64".
$ dir /s /b C:\work\b4\oc-cpu | find /c /v ""
0
=> npm rolled the install back: no opencode.exe at all, so no PE machine to read. The cause is opencode-ai's
   postinstall.mjs: it picks the platform package from os.arch() of the node that runs it (arm64 here), so it only
   accepts opencode-windows-arm64, which --cpu=x64 left out. (On an x64 node it would also probe AVX2:
   IsProcessorFeaturePresent(40) is False on this VM from Arm PowerShell.)

